Z||000000||jch82||11-10-2001||01:24 AM||||First off, is it possible? If so, how much would something like that cost for 17"rims?? When I buy rims for the fiero, I was thinking of white rims...Would it even be worth it to do? Any info is appreciated!! Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||artherd||11-10-2001||01:43 AM||||Should cost $1-200 from a good shop for all 4.  Get it done by a place that knows what they're doing (prep is KEY.) and they'll look and wear great.<P>Powder coat stands up unbelivabely well to abuse from rocks/etc.  It basically will not chip (it's slightly elastic when cured)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||11-10-2001||02:53 AM||||The above price is right on the money.<BR>There's a shop right near me that does powdercoating and the owner told me it would cost about $50.00 a wheel.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||04:46 AM||||Im pretty sure most factory painted wheels are powder coated. Theres no paint process more durable. too bad they dont do car bodies. Motorcycle frames are too for the most part.||||reg||1
Z||000004||donalson||11-10-2001||04:53 AM||||a friend of mine did his wheels in gun metal black w/ a home kit...only thign is you can't inhale the stuff it's deadly, and you've gota find an old oven that won't ever be used for cooking in EVER again...<P>i think the DIY kit was about $40 or so...they looked real good when he was done...still do...I'd like to do them to my wheels one day...just a matter of finding that oven *grin*<P>mark<P>------------------<BR>'86 mr2 hardtop<P>mid-engine lover||||reg||1
Z||000005||avengador1||11-10-2001||11:53 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.eastwoodcompany.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eastwoodcompany.com</A>  has HotCoat powder coating equipment including the infrared heat lamps to cure larger parts if you are willing to spend the money (maybe do it as a side business <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
